import json

with open('/tmp/report_data.json') as f:
    d = json.load(f)

html = '''<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Global Intentional Homicide Trends: A Multi-Dimensional Analysis (1990–2023)</title>
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js@4.4.0/dist/chart.umd.min.js"></script>
<style>
  :root {
    --primary: #1a2e4a;
    --accent: #c94f4f;
    --accent2: #3a7bd5;
    --success: #2d9e6b;
    --warn: #e07b39;
    --bg: #f7f8fa;
    --card: #ffffff;
    --text: #1e2835;
    --muted: #6b7a8d;
    --border: #dde3ec;
    --kpi-bg: #1a2e4a;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.6; }

  /* Header */
  .report-header {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2e4a 0%, #2a4870 100%);
    color: white;
    padding: 48px 40px 40px;
  }
  .report-header .meta { font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; color: #a0b4cc; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .report-header h1 { font-size: 28px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.3; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .report-header .subtitle { font-size: 15px; color: #c0d0e0; max-width: 680px; }
  .source-tag { display: inline-block; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.12); border-radius: 4px; padding: 4px 10px; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 1px; text-transform: uppercase; margin-top: 16px; color: #a0b4cc; }

  /* Layout */
  .container { max-width: 1120px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 32px 60px; }

  /* KPI Dashboard */
  .kpi-section {
    background: var(--primary);
    padding: 32px 40px;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .kpi-section .kpi-title { color: #a0b4cc; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .kpi-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr); gap: 1px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1); border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; }
  .kpi-card { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.05); padding: 20px 16px; text-align: center; }
  .kpi-card .kpi-value { font-size: 30px; font-weight: 700; color: #fff; line-height: 1; }
  .kpi-card .kpi-value.accent { color: #ff7070; }
  .kpi-card .kpi-value.success { color: #5dd899; }
  .kpi-card .kpi-value.warn { color: #f0a857; }
  .kpi-card .kpi-label { font-size: 11px; color: #a0b4cc; margin-top: 6px; line-height: 1.4; }
  .kpi-card .kpi-sub { font-size: 10px; color: #6b88a8; margin-top: 4px; }

  /* Content */
  .content-grid { margin-top: 32px; display: grid; gap: 24px; }

  /* Section */
  .section { background: var(--card); border-radius: 10px; border: 1px solid var(--border); overflow: hidden; }
  .section-header { padding: 20px 28px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; }
  .section-num { font-size: 11px; color: var(--accent2); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .section-header h2 { font-size: 18px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--primary); }
  .section-body { padding: 24px 28px; }

  /* Charts */
  .chart-wrap { position: relative; }
  .chart-wrap canvas { max-height: 320px; }
  .chart-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 24px; }

  /* Text */
  p { font-size: 14px; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .insight { background: #f0f4ff; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent2); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0; font-size: 13px; margin: 12px 0; color: #1a2e4a; }
  .warning { background: #fff7f0; border-left: 3px solid var(--warn); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0; font-size: 13px; margin: 12px 0; }

  /* Tables */
  .two-col { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 24px; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 13px; }
  th { background: #f0f4f8; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.5px; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 8px 12px; text-align: left; }
  td { padding: 8px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
  .rank { color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; width: 28px; }
  .rate-high { color: #c94f4f; font-weight: 700; }
  .rate-low { color: #2d9e6b; font-weight: 700; }
  .rate-bar { display: inline-block; height: 6px; border-radius: 3px; vertical-align: middle; margin-left: 8px; }

  /* Footnote */
  .footnote { font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding-top: 12px; margin-top: 8px; }

  /* Limitations */
  .limitations-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; margin-top: 8px; }
  .limit-card { background: #fafbfd; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 14px 16px; }
  .limit-card h4 { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--primary); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .limit-card p { font-size: 13px; margin: 0; color: var(--muted); }

  /* Policy recs */
  .rec-list { list-style: none; margin-top: 8px; }
  .rec-list li { padding: 10px 14px; border-left: 3px solid var(--success); background: #f4fbf7; border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0; margin-bottom: 8px; font-size: 13px; }
  .rec-list li strong { color: var(--primary); display: block; margin-bottom: 2px; }

  /* Notable trends */
  .trend-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; }
  .trend-card { border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; }
  .trend-card .trend-header { padding: 10px 14px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 1px; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .trend-card.decrease .trend-header { background: #edf7f2; color: #2d9e6b; }
  .trend-card.increase .trend-header { background: #fdf0f0; color: #c94f4f; }
  .trend-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 13px; }
  .trend-table th { background: #f7f8fa; color: var(--muted); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.5px; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 6px 12px; }
  .trend-table td { padding: 7px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .trend-table tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
  .chg-pos { color: #c94f4f; font-weight: 600; }
  .chg-neg { color: #2d9e6b; font-weight: 600; }

  /* Footer */
  .report-footer { background: var(--primary); color: #6b88a8; text-align: center; padding: 20px; font-size: 12px; margin-top: 40px; }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .kpi-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
    .chart-grid, .two-col, .limitations-grid, .trend-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .container { padding: 0 16px 40px; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="report-header">
  <div style="max-width:1120px; margin:0 auto; padding:0 32px;">
    <div class="meta">UNODC Crime Trends Survey &nbsp;|&nbsp; Policy Analysis Report</div>
    <h1>Global Intentional Homicide Trends:<br>A Multi-Dimensional Analysis (1990–2023)</h1>
    <div class="subtitle">A comprehensive trend analysis of intentional homicide rates across 201 countries, disaggregated by sex and age group over three decades. Prepared for policy analysts and public safety stakeholders.</div>
    <span class="source-tag">Data Source: UNODC Crime Trends Survey (CTS) via Kaggle</span>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="kpi-section">
  <div style="max-width:1120px; margin:0 auto; padding:0 8px;">
    <div class="kpi-title">Executive KPI Dashboard &mdash; Reference Year 2022</div>
    <div class="kpi-grid">
      <div class="kpi-card">
        <div class="kpi-value">''' + str(d['kpi_median']) + '''</div>
        <div class="kpi-label">Global Median Homicide Rate</div>
        <div class="kpi-sub">per 100,000 population (2022)</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kpi-card">
        <div class="kpi-value accent">''' + str(d['kpi_ratio']) + '''×</div>
        <div class="kpi-label">Male-to-Female Homicide Ratio</div>
        <div class="kpi-sub">Males face 2.6× higher risk (2022)</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kpi-card">
        <div class="kpi-value accent">76.3</div>
        <div class="kpi-label">Highest National Rate</div>
        <div class="kpi-sub">Turks & Caicos Islands (2022)</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kpi-card">
        <div class="kpi-value success">−9.6%</div>
        <div class="kpi-label">2000s → 2010s Avg Change</div>
        <div class="kpi-sub">Global mean homicide rate fell</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kpi-card">
        <div class="kpi-value warn">53%</div>
        <div class="kpi-label">Reporting Coverage Rate</div>
        <div class="kpi-sub">106 / 201 countries in 2022</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="container">
<div class="content-grid">

<!-- Section 1: Global Overview -->
<div class="section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="section-num">01</span>
    <h2>Global Homicide Rate Overview</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="section-body">
    <p>The global intentional homicide rate has followed a complex trajectory over the past three decades. Analyzing the median rate across all reporting countries — a robust measure that resists distortion from extreme outliers — reveals a general declining trend from 1990 to the present, punctuated by periods of stagnation and reversal.</p>

    <div class="chart-grid" style="margin: 20px 0;">
      <div class="chart-wrap">
        <canvas id="globalTrendChart"></canvas>
      </div>
      <div class="chart-wrap">
        <canvas id="coverageChart"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="insight">The global <strong>median homicide rate fell from 3.35 (1990) to 2.27 per 100,000 (2022)</strong>, a reduction of approximately 32%. However, the global mean — heavily influenced by high-rate countries in Latin America and the Caribbean — has remained persistently elevated, declining only modestly from ~8.3 in the 1990s to ~7.7 in the 2010s.</div>

    <p>The 2000s–2010s transition saw the sharpest improvement: the global average fell <strong>9.6%</strong> between these decades. The 2010s–2020s transition showed near-stagnation (<strong>+0.2%</strong>), suggesting the pace of improvement has slowed considerably. Decade averages: 1990s = ''' + str(d['avg_90s']) + ''', 2000s = ''' + str(d['avg_00s']) + ''', 2010s = ''' + str(d['avg_10s']) + ''', 2020s = ''' + str(d['avg_20s']) + '''.</p>

    <p>Reporting coverage expanded substantially from 94 countries in 1990 to a peak of 162 in 2008, then declined to 84 by 2023 — a reporting gap effect that analysts must account for when interpreting recent trends.</p>
    <div class="footnote">Note: Declining coverage in recent years (especially 2022–2023) means recent global statistics are based on a smaller and potentially non-representative sample of countries.</div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Section 2: Regional & Country Comparison -->
<div class="section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="section-num">02</span>
    <h2>Regional &amp; Country-Level Comparison</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="section-body">
    <div class="chart-wrap" style="margin-bottom:20px;">
      <canvas id="regionalChart" style="max-height:280px;"></canvas>
    </div>

    <p>Geographic disparities in homicide rates are stark and persistent. <strong>Latin America and the Caribbean</strong> consistently records the highest median rates globally — more than 10× higher than Europe. Africa occupies a middle position, while Asia and Europe show the lowest rates among major regions.</p>

    <div class="insight">Latin America's median homicide rate in 2023 (~17.8 per 100,000) is approximately <strong>20× higher than Europe's median (~0.9)</strong>, illustrating the profound regional inequality in homicide risk.</div>

    <div class="two-col" style="margin-top:20px;">
      <div>
        <h3 style="font-size:13px; color:var(--accent); font-weight:700; margin-bottom:10px; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:1px;">Top 10 Highest Rates (Most Recent Year)</h3>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Country</th><th>Year</th><th>Rate</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
'''

for i, (c, yr, rate) in enumerate(d['top10'], 1):
    bar_w = int(rate / 80 * 80)
    html += f'<tr><td class="rank">{i}</td><td>{c}</td><td style="color:var(--muted)">{yr}</td><td><span class="rate-high">{rate:.1f}</span><span class="rate-bar" style="width:{bar_w}px; background:#ffcccc;"></span></td></tr>\n'

html += '''          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 style="font-size:13px; color:var(--success); font-weight:700; margin-bottom:10px; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:1px;">Bottom 10 Lowest Rates (Most Recent Year)</h3>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Country</th><th>Year</th><th>Rate</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
'''

for i, (c, yr, rate) in enumerate(d['bottom10'], 1):
    html += f'<tr><td class="rank">{i}</td><td>{c}</td><td style="color:var(--muted)">{yr}</td><td class="rate-low">{rate:.4f}</td></tr>\n'

html += '''          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="footnote" style="margin-top:12px;">Most recent available year shown per country. Small island territories with limited populations (e.g., Turks and Caicos, St. Kitts) may show extreme rates due to small absolute numbers amplified by population normalization. Qatar and Singapore represent the safest jurisdictions with rates below 0.07 per 100,000.</div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Section 3: Gender Disparity -->
<div class="section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="section-num">03</span>
    <h2>Gender Disparity in Homicide Victimization</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="section-body">
    <p>One of the most consistent findings in global homicide data is the pronounced overrepresentation of male victims. Across virtually every country and year in this dataset, males face dramatically higher homicide rates than females — a pattern that persists across all regions and income levels.</p>

    <div class="chart-grid" style="margin: 20px 0;">
      <div class="chart-wrap">
        <canvas id="genderTrendChart"></canvas>
      </div>
      <div class="chart-wrap">
        <canvas id="ratioChart"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="insight"><strong>Key Finding:</strong> In 2022, the global median male homicide rate was approximately <strong>2.86 per 100,000</strong>, compared to <strong>1.10 per 100,000 for females</strong> — a male-to-female ratio of <strong>2.6×</strong>. This ratio has persisted throughout the entire observation period, ranging from 2.5× to nearly 5.7× in select years.</div>

    <p>The ratio shows considerable year-to-year variation, partly reflecting changing country composition in reporting. The spike observed in 1993 (ratio ~5.7) reflects a period when only ~44 countries reported sex-disaggregated data, skewing the sample. As coverage expanded post-2000, the ratio stabilized in the 2.6–4.0 range.</p>

    <div class="warning"><strong>Policy Implication:</strong> Male homicide overrepresentation cannot be treated as a reason to deprioritize female victimization. Femicide and intimate partner violence require distinct policy responses that go beyond aggregate rate comparisons. Sex-disaggregated data collection remains inconsistent across countries, limiting more precise analysis.</div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Section 4: Age Group Analysis -->
<div class="section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="section-num">04</span>
    <h2>Age Group Analysis</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="section-body">
    <p>Age-disaggregated data reveals that homicide risk is highly concentrated in specific life stages. Young adults face disproportionately high victimization rates, while children and the elderly are comparatively less at risk — though still significant in absolute terms.</p>

    <div class="chart-wrap" style="margin: 20px 0;">
      <canvas id="ageChart" style="max-height:300px;"></canvas>
    </div>

    <div class="insight"><strong>Peak Risk Ages 25–44:</strong> The 25–29 and 30–44 age groups show the highest median homicide rates for both males and females globally. For males, the median rate in the 30–44 bracket is <strong>4.08 per 100,000</strong>, compared to just <strong>2.12</strong> for those 60 and older.</div>

    <p>The 15–29 age cohort (spanning brackets 15–17, 18–19, 20–24, 25–29) collectively represents the highest-risk window, consistent with global research linking youth homicide to gang activity, organized crime, and interpersonal conflict in high-inequality settings. The gender gap widens sharply in the 18–29 range, where male rates are 3–4× female rates.</p>

    <p>Children aged 0–9 exhibit very low but non-negligible rates (male median: 0.48, female: 0.37), reflecting infanticide and child abuse-related homicides. The relative gender parity in this group contrasts sharply with the divergence in adult age brackets.</p>

    <div class="footnote">Note: Age-disaggregated data has significantly lower coverage than aggregate (ALL) data. Results reflect the subset of countries reporting detailed age breakdowns and may not be globally representative.</div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Section 5: Notable Trends -->
<div class="section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="section-num">05</span>
    <h2>Notable Country-Level Trends &amp; Outliers</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="section-body">
    <p>Among countries with at least 10 years of continuous data, the trajectories below represent the most dramatic transformations — both positive and negative — in homicide rates over the observation period.</p>

    <div class="trend-grid" style="margin-top:16px;">
      <div class="trend-card decrease">
        <div class="trend-header">Biggest Decreases</div>
        <table class="trend-table">
